*
# Deny-by-default, the same mechanic .gitignore documents: `*` ignores
# everything, and each rule below names back exactly what the image build
# COPYs. The builder does not look inside a directory it has already
# ignored, so every kept directory is re-opened (`!dir/`), its contents
# denied again (`dir/*`), and its files named back by a glob SCOPED to that
# directory — that scoping is what stops a `!*.py` from reaching into a
# directory the build never copies. `.git`, `.venv`, `node_modules` and
# `tests/` stay denied with no rule of their own: nothing the build COPYs
# lives in them, and a file the build needs but no rule names back simply
# never enters the context.

# ---- repository root ------------------------------------------------------
!/VERSION

# ---- backend/ — the app, its requirements and the schema files ------------
!backend/
backend/*
!backend/*.py
!backend/*.sql
!backend/requirements.txt

# ---- public/ — static assets served at / -----------------------------------
!public/
public/*
!public/*.css
!public/*.html
!public/favicon.ico

# ---- src/ — browser modules served at /src/* -------------------------------
!src/
src/*
!src/*.js
!src/*.jsx
!src/*.json
!src/views/
src/views/*
!src/views/*.jsx

# ---- scripts/plots/ — the /api/export render script (backend/api_export.py) -
# The repo tooling under scripts/ stays out; only the three plot modules the
# export subprocess runs come in, reopened and named back the same way
# .gitignore's scripts/plots block does it.
!/scripts/
scripts/*
!scripts/plots/
scripts/plots/*
!scripts/plots/*.py
